    example: "A small skincare counter uses one dropper bottle. The reel is 20 seconds. In the first three seconds the bottle fills the frame, the label is blank, and the voice says Two drops, morning. An adult hand takes two drops and the cap goes back on. No face. No second bottle. A still that printed a crest was rejected. A version with a transformed face was rejected. The caption names the shop and the size of the bottle. The night oil waits for another reel.",
    bridge: "Scro's product promo keeps one product, a blank label, and no fake logo. The shop name goes in the caption. Approve the still so the cap matches your photo, show one use, and export the vertical reel. Adult hands can show that single step. A face is not required, and a generated skin change is rejected before it renders. The other step in the routine is another post. Read the caption on a phone and confirm the shop name and the size are there, while the picture stays one bottle with a blank label.",
